---
// AboutUnderground.astro
// Block: > THE UNDERGROUND MAN — quote block + decorative green side cell
import "../../styles/about-underground.css";
---

<div class="about__block-row">
  <div class="about__block about__block--quote">
    <div class="about__label-row">
      <div class="about__icon-wrapper">
        <span class="about__icon" aria-hidden="true">&gt;</span>
      </div>
      <h3 class="about__label">THE UNDERGROUND MAN</h3>
    </div>
    <p class="about__body-text">
      It is clear to me now that, owing to my unbounded curiosity and to the
      high standard I set for myself, I often looked at code with furious
      discontent, which verged on loathing, and so I inwardly attributed the
      same feeling to everyone's PRs.
    </p>
  </div>
  <!-- Decorative green side cell (rightS2 equivalent ~150px) -->
  <div class="about__decorative-cell" aria-hidden="true"></div>
</div>
